# Zed Remote Indexing Marker

This file enables remote indexing in Zed editor.

Project: PsychoNoir-Kontrapunkt
Created: 2025
Purpose: Enable seamless remote development and indexing without git noise

## Configuration Notes
- This marker file is tracked in git (root-level file policy)
- Git is configured to ignore subdirectories per .gitignore
- Only root-level files are tracked to minimize source control spam
- Remote indexing will respect .gitignore and file_scan_exclusions in .zed/settings.json

## Indexed Directories (via .zed/settings.json)
Remote indexing will scan only configured paths, excluding:
- node_modules/
- .venv/
- __pycache__/
- Large codebase directories
- Build artifacts

This ensures clean, fast indexing without overwhelming git suggestions.
